{
 "id": "caster-fork-petg",
 "brief": "The fork of a small cart caster in PETG on an FDM printer (choose the print orientation). Its top face (z = 0) sits under the cart and is held by four M4 screws that come down from the cart into heat-set inserts (5.6 mm) in the fork at (x +-18, y +-12), 6 mm deep. The wheel is 44 mm in diameter and 16 mm wide on an 8 mm axle along Y, centred at z = -50; the axle slips into the fork from the side. Keep the fork inside x = -25 to 25, y = -18 to 18, z = -62 to 0. Each caster carries up to 30 kg and the cart gets dropped off kerbs (factor 2); in a turn the wheel also sees 150 N along the axle, and when it hits a lip 150 N along X, each with half the vertical load. Safety factor 2.5.",
